## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical APIM quota implementation and OpenAI routing for multi-tenant SaaS architectures.

## Key Concepts
- API Management policies with rate-limit-by-key
- Tenant-scoped routing via request headers
- Telemetry integration with Application Insights

## Code Example
```xml
<policies>
  <inbound>
    <base />
    <set-variable name='TenantID' value='@(context.Request.Headers.GetValueOrDefault("x-tenant-id","default"))' />
    <rate-limit-by-key calls='60' renewal-period='60' key='@(context.Variables["TenantID"])' />
  </inbound>
</policies>
```

```javascript
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tenantId = req.headers['x-tenant-id'] || 'default';
  const startTime = Date.now();

  try {
    const response = await callOpenAI(req.body);

    // Log usage to Application Insights
    context.log('TenantUsage', {
      tenantId,
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
      duration: Date.now() - startTime,
      status: 'success'
    });

    return { status: 200, body: response };
  } catch (error) {
    context.log.error('TenantError', { tenantId, error: error.message });
    return { status: 500, body: { error: 'Service unavailable' } };
  }
};
```

## Validation Approach
Test with multiple tenant IDs using load testing tools, verify rate limits trigger at 60 requests/minute per tenant, and confirm telemetry appears in Application Insights queries.

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design a comprehensive Azure OpenAI solution that integrates multiple Azure services while addressing key enterprise requirements like multilingual support, data governance, and cost management in a beginner-friendly scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Language detection and per-tenant language preference management
- Per-language knowledge bases stored in Azure Blob Storage
- Real-time translation layer and content grounding via Azure Cognitive Search
- PII redaction and per-tenant budget enforcement mechanisms
- API Management routing policies and comprehensive auditing to Azure Data Lake

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: detect language, translate, search knowledge base, query OpenAI, translate back
const lang = detectLanguage(request);
const kb = await loadLanguageKB(lang);
const translatedQuery = await translateToEnglish(request, lang);
const groundedContext = await cognitiveSearch(translatedQuery, kb);
const response = await callOpenAI(groundedContext);
return translateFromEnglish(response, lang);
```

